+++
title: Creativity resources
pointers: Start with 10 minutes, not 2 hours. | Track streaks, not perfection. | Share unfinished work on purpose.
teaser: Most of what stops a creative practice isn't a skills problem — these are the small structural fixes that tend to actually move it.
+++

This page isn't just for people ready to book a session — if you're
curious about the practice of creative work and want to look around
before (or instead of) working with anyone here, this is for you too.

Notes on staying in a creative practice long enough for it to matter:
what a creative block usually actually is, how to structure practice time
so it survives a busy week, and how to share unfinished work without it
costing you the will to finish it.

Below is a running, personal collection — books, talks, and papers our
coaches actually go back to, each tagged with who recommends it, not a
generic reading list assembled for the page.
